</tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Acetate production</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">42.7<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t4-fn3"><sup>b</sup></xref></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">42.2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">42.1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Methane evolution</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">21.6</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">21.7</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">21.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Formate exchange rate</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">10.6</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">10.8</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">10.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Hydrogen exchange rate</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">79.4</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">79.2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">79.9</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>D. vulgaris</italic> biomass</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.255<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t4-fn4"><sup>c</sup></xref></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.255</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.254</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>M. maripaludis</italic> biomass</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.103</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.125</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.126</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Ratio D:M</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.48</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.04</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.02</td></tr></tbody></table><graphic alternate-form-of="t4" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="msb4100131-t4"/><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t4-fn1" fn-type="footnote"><p>Acetate consumption by <italic>M. maripaludis</italic> and formate and hydrogen accumulation were set to 0. Lactate uptake rate was 48 &#x003bc;mol/h.</p></fn><fn id="t4-fn2" fn-type="footnote"><p>&#x02018;D' and &#x02018;M' are <italic>D. vulgaris</italic> and <italic>M. maripaludis</italic>, respectively. 1.0, 0, and 0.5 refer to the distribution of biomass maximization between species, with the combination of 1.0 and 0 indicating that only one species biomass should be optimized, and 0.5 and 0.5 indicating that biomass production by each species should be equally optimized.</p></fn><fn id="t4-fn3" fn-type="footnote"><p>All metabolite fluxes are in &#x003bc;mol/h.</p></fn><fn id="t4-fn4" fn-type="footnote"><p>Biomass fluxes are in units of mg DCW/h.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Comparison of key flux ratios in <italic>D. vulgaris</italic> for monoculture as compared to co-culture</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>D. vulgaris</italic>/<italic>M. maripaludis</italic> co-culture</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">Form/H<sub>2</sub></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">Ace/Lac</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">PFL/POR</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">PYC/ME</th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">24 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.15</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.63</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.93</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">50 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.15</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.42</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.95</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">56 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.15</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.42</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.95</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">61.5 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.13</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.17</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.96</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">68.5 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.14</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.15</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.93</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">76 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.14</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.10</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.85</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">100 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.14</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.92</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.10</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.85</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>D. vulgaris</italic> monoculture</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">8 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.90/0.81<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t5-fn2"><sup>a</sup></xref></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.83/1.94</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.32/3.41</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">12 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.83/0.80</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.72/1.82</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.35/3.36</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">16 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.79/0.82</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.67/1.81</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">4.0/3.39</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">24 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.77/0.81</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.71/1.87</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.93/3.36</td></tr></tbody></table><graphic alternate-form-of="t5" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="msb4100131-t5"/><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t5-fn1" fn-type="footnote"><p>ME, NADP-dependent malic enzyme; POR, pyruvate oxidoreductase; PFL, pyruvate-formate lyase; PYC, pyruvate carboxylase.</p></fn><fn id="t5-fn2" fn-type="footnote"><p>The first value is for model simulation constrained by experimental lactate and sulfate measurements, whereas second value is for simulation constrained by experimental lactate and hydrogen.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t6" position="float"><label>Table 6</label><caption><p>ATP maintenance requirement for each organism in co-culture, matching individual biomass production rates to those estimated experimentally</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Time of growth</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x003bc;mol/h<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t6-fn1"><sup>a</sup></xref> <italic>D. vulgaris</italic></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x003bc;mol/(h mg DCW)<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t6-fn2"><sup>b</sup></xref> <italic>D. vulgaris</italic></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x003bc;mol/h<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t6-fn1"><sup>a</sup></xref> <italic>M. maripaludis</italic></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x003bc;mol/(h mg DCW)<xref ref-type="fn" rid="t6-fn2"><sup>b</sup></xref> <italic>M. maripaludis</italic></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">24 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.077</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.3</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.35</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">50 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.6</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.32</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.0</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">61.5 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">8.2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.36</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">2.6</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.86</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">76 h</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">10.2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.18</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">6.2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.80</td></tr></tbody></table><graphic alternate-form-of="t6" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="msb4100131-t6"/><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t6-fn1" fn-type="footnote"><p>Value of ATP hydrolysis reaction flux in each organism.</p></fn><fn id="t6-fn2" fn-type="footnote"><p>Rate of ATP hydrolysis normalized by the amount of biomass in each organism present at the sample time. Biomass concentration was estimated by culture OD (<xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="S1">Supplementary Figure 1A</xref>) and the cell ratio of the two organisms (<xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="S1">Supplementary Figure 1B</xref>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec><ack><p>We thank G Pinchuk, R Thauer, H Toyama, J Dodsworth, and J Wall for their thoughtful discussion of our work, M Sadilek for his invaluable assistance in performing the GC&#x02013;MS and HPLC analyses, B Zuniga for excellent technical assistance, and S Flagan for her help in preparing <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1</xref>. We also thank Mr Everett Short for supplying us with the photograph in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1</xref>. This work was supported by the Department of Energy's Office of Biological and Environmental Sciences under the GTL-Genomics Program via the Virtual Institute for Microbial Stress and Survival (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://VIMSS.lbl.gov">http://VIMSS.lbl.gov</ext-link>). John Leigh was supported by Department of Energy Basic Research for the Hydrogen Fuel Initiative grant DE-FG02-05ER15709, and by grant NCC 2-1273 from the NASA Astrobiology Institute.</p></ack><ref-list><ref id="b1"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Blanch</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name> (<year>1996</year>) <source>Biochemical Engineering</source>. New York, NY: Marcel Dekker</citation></ref><ref id="b2"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Boetius